1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Three thousand forty four Indian startup

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,800
funding rounds. Thirty eight billion dollars.

3
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:06,000
And 979 of them with no disclosed amount.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,800
979 rows have no amount.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
4 have unparseable dates.

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,000
Most projects delete those and move on.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,200
21 cities, 70 industry labels,

8
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:19,000
37 investment types.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
All normalized by hand. Bangalore and Bengaluru
are the same city.

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,500
One SQLite table, four views,

11
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,500
thirteen analysis queries.

12
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,000
Then the same thing again in Power BI.

13
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,200
Random Forest won, and it won on cross validation
inside the training window.

14
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:39,000
RMSLE 1.27 against a 2.43 dummy baseline.

15
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
R squared is negative. I'm showing you that number too.

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,500
Random Forest scored higher on the test set.

17
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,500
I didn't pick it, because it lost on cross validation.

18
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,000
Picking it on test would have been fitting the answer I wanted.

19
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,200
Classification splits rounds into low, medium and high.

20
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:57,500
Thresholds from training percentiles only.

21
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:00,000
Clustering lands on three segments. 2,062 events.

22
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,500
Permutation importance and SHAP. Investment type dominates.

23
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,500
Most other features are near zero, or negative.

24
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,000
Investor features made it worse, so they ship disabled.

25
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,500
Ten dashboard pages.

26
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,500
161 tests.

27
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:20,000
A scheduled runner that skips itself when the CSV hasn't changed.

28
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,500
A PDF generated from the live metrics, so the figures can't drift.

29
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,500
Analytical prototype. Not investment advice.

30
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,000
Which piece would you want the code for?
